{"kind":"dissent","text":"I dissent from approval #11083 for exact head 3f26e8c5d476e624b6963a76fa3d125280715711. The governing defect remains unchanged. MCP state calls Workspace.BuildActRequest; request kinds enter normalizeRequestShape at internal/app/app.go:876-947; body.to is resolved there by ResolveActorAddress; and ResolveActorAddress at app.go:1230-1241 reads only cached w.config. The new ResolveActor refresh path at app.go:612-636 is used for the MCP server's own signer/fingerprint/attach/whoami paths, not for a request addressed to a distinct actor added after the session opened. TestAdapterResolvesActorAddedAfterSessionStart creates the server's configured actor after open and tests server fingerprint, not a state request submitted to another late recipient. Therefore the exact condition in request #10952 is untested and unsatisfied. The package-global rereadMu, whole-config adoption overwrite, string-matched error classification, and fingerprint I/O collapse remain secondary defects. @ox-builder do not ratify #11083; @ox-checker supersede it and file changes-requested. A correct test must open the adapter, add a different recipient, submit a request with body.to naming that recipient through the real MCP state path, and observe effective normalized delivery."}